{"id":"000VIL","title":"Rotation Sequence","author":"Nelyn","solvedCount":1,"difficulty":5,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-17T17:33:19+00:00","posted":"am 15. Oktober 2026, 23:56 Uhr","rules":"Rotation Sequence\n\n+\n\nTHE RULES\n\nNormal Sudoku\n\nNormal Sudoku rules apply.\n\nPositive Diagonal\n\nThe digits cannot repeat on the positive diagonal.\n\nConcentric Rings Rotation\n\nThe grid is divided into four concentric square rings, labelled A (outermost) to D (innermost).\n\nEach number in the sequence rotates its indicated ring and all rings outside it.\n\nThe number gives the distance moved in cells along each affected ring's perimeter:\n→ clockwise, ← counterclockwise.\n\nThe centre cell remains fixed.\n\nFINAL ROTATION\n\nAfter applying the entire sequence, the four rings must form one coherent rotation of the original grid, meaning either 0°, 90°, 180°, or 270°.\n\nThe digits to put in the grid are the ones before the rotation !\n\nBoth the original and resulting grids must satisfy all Sudoku rules and all constraints, even the clues between the grid and the sequence above the grid.\n\nThe sequence must be filled with the digits 1 to 9 exactly once each.\n\nRegion Sum Lockout Lines\n\nEach purple line follows both rules:\n\nRegion Sum: The digits on each segment of the line, separated by 3×3 box boundaries, must have the same sum (counting diamond ends).\n\nLockout: The digits in the two endpoint diamonds must differ by at least 4. Digits along the line cannot have values strictly between the two endpoint digits.\n\nKropki Dots\n\nDigits separated by a white dot must be consecutive.\n\nArrow\n\nDigits on an arrow line sum to the digit in the bulb attached.\n\n▶ PLAY","solutionCode":"Row 7 left to right","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/rp613d90px","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"link":"https://sudokupad.app/rp613d90px","linkKind":"sudokupad","attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-17T20:41:39+00:00","settings":{},"summary":{"f